target_text:
And surely, into your saintly dreaming, there slid the
musk of a Vision’s mouth;

Carnations carried a cup of perfume, foamed by winds
of the amorous South;

The lively bee with his tawny body matched the brown
of your gabardine;

Betwixt the curve of your sleeping Angers the grass
blades broke in a sheaf of green;

The dews of the night were pearled upon you, dews
that the noon sun drank at last;

And the summer rains cooled your ferny pillow; the
arms of the twilight held you fast.

